                <pb facs="0227" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg213"/>

                <head>Ecuador and Peru</head>
                <p>[For previous correspondence on this subject, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1941v06/pg_212">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1941, volume VI, pages
                        212</ref> ff. For protocol between Ecuador and Peru regarding peace,
                    friendship, and boundaries (signed also by representatives of the United States,
                    Argentina, Brazil, and Chile), signed at Rio de Janeiro, January 29, 1942, see
                    Department of State Executive Agreement Series No. 288, or 56 Stat. (pt. 2)
                    1818. Correspondence for 1944 regarding the Aranha formula, the Argentine’s
                    unrecognized government as a guarantor power, and the reports concerning
                    Peruvian forces on the border is not published.]</p>
            </div>
